---
globs:
  - "src/agentWork/**"
  - "src/review/**"
  - "src/agent/**"
  - "src/prWorkspace/**"
  - "src/effect/**"
  - "src/github/**"
  - "test/prSurfaceImportGraph.test.ts"
  - "test/architectureRules.test.ts"
  - "test/prSurface.seam.test.ts"
---
Route PR GitHub I/O through `createPrSurface` / `PrSurface` (`src/github/prSurface.ts`, ADR 0026). `test/architectureRules.test.ts` keeps `@octokit/*` imports inside `src/github/` and rejects exported `token: string`, `expiresAtTs`, or `tokenExpiresAtTs` parameters outside `src/github/` and the `src/prWorkspace/` checkout credential seam. `test/prSurfaceImportGraph.test.ts` keeps `installationOctokit` references inside those seams and covers the guard helpers. Work items store `installationId`, and the worker mints the token inside the seam at execution time. `gitCredentialAuth()` is the only credential escape, used for clone and push. Leased executors receive the epoch-aware surface so each method in `PR_SURFACE_MUTATION_METHODS` runs inside the operation-intent boundary and recovers through `recoverPrSurfaceMutation.ts`; never import `prSurfaceImpl.ts` from feature or worker code. `PrSurface` stays a set of raw GitHub reads and writes: feature-specific assembly (prior-feedback thread
